sentences.t:
Tum variae comitum facies, immania cete,
et senior Glauci chorus, Inousque Palaemon,
Tritonesque citi, Phorcique exercitus omnis;

sentences.l:
Then the various faces of the companions, huge sea-monsters,
and the older chorus of Glaucus, and Ino's Palaemon,
and the swift Tritons, and all the army of Phorcus;

sentences.t:
et super incumbens cum puppis parte revolsa,
cumque gubernaclo, liquidas proiecit in undas
praecipitem ac socios nequiquam saepe vocantem;

sentences.l:
and leaning over with part of the stern torn off,
and with the helm, into the liquid waves he threw him
headlong, and his comrades in vain often calling;
